# Christian Concern News Monitor — Free Edition

A hands-off news monitor that checks UK newspaper and Christian press RSS
feeds every hour, flags articles relevant to your issues (assisted
dying, abortion, Islam, religious liberty, etc.), and can post a digest
to Slack and/or email it to you.

**Cost: £0/month** for this version. It runs on GitHub's free Actions
service, so nothing needs to be installed on your laptop and nothing
needs to stay switched on.

## What's in this folder

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `monitor.py` | The actual script — fetches feeds, classifies, sends alerts |
| `feeds.yaml` | List of RSS feeds to check (edit this to add/remove sources) |
| `issues.yaml` | Keyword lists per issue (edit this to tune what counts as relevant) |
| `requirements.txt` | The one dependency needed (PyYAML) |
| `.github/workflows/monitor.yml` | Tells GitHub to run the script every hour, for free |
| `seen_articles.json` | Tracks which articles have already been reported (starts empty) |

## One-time setup (15–20 minutes, no coding needed)

1. **Create a free GitHub account** at github.com if you don't already have one.
2. **Create a new repository** (Settings can be "Private" — that's fine, GitHub
   Actions is still free on private repos for a generous monthly allowance).
3. **Upload this whole folder** to that repository. Easiest way: on the
   repo page, click "Add file" → "Upload files", drag in everything from
   this folder (including the hidden `.github` folder — if your file
   browser hides it, use GitHub Desktop or ask a colleague with basic git
   familiarity to push it for you).
4. **Get a free Guardian API key** (optional but recommended): register at
   https://open-platform.theguardian.com/access/ — instant, free, no card.
5. **Add your keys as repository secrets** (Settings → Secrets and
   variables → Actions → "New repository secret"):
   - `GUARDIAN_API_KEY` — from step 4
   - `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` — if you want Slack alerts (see below)
   - `EMAIL_ENABLED`, `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`,
     `EMAIL_FROM`, `EMAIL_TO` — if you want email alerts (see below)
   - `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — only if you want the optional AI-classification
     upgrade later (not required to run this for free)
6. That's it. GitHub will now run the check every hour automatically. You
   can also trigger it manually any time from the repo's "Actions" tab →
   "News Monitor" → "Run workflow".

## Getting a free Slack webhook (optional)

Slack → your workspace → "Apps" → search "Incoming Webhooks" → add to a
channel → copy the webhook URL it gives you → paste that as the
`SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` secret above.

## Getting email working (optional)

Any SMTP-capable email account works. For a free Gmail account:
- `SMTP_HOST` = smtp.gmail.com
- `SMTP_PORT` = 465
- `SMTP_USER` = your Gmail address
- `SMTP_PASS` = a Gmail **App Password** (Google Account → Security →
  2-Step Verification → App Passwords) — not your normal password
- `EMAIL_ENABLED` = true
- `EMAIL_FROM` / `EMAIL_TO` = the addresses to send from/to

Ask your IT/comms team if they'd prefer to use the organisation's own
email account instead of a personal Gmail — same settings, different host.

## Tuning it

- **Add more sources:** add entries to `feeds.yaml`. Most news sites'
  RSS feeds are at `[site]/rss` or similar — search "[site name] RSS feed".
- **Add more keywords:** edit `issues.yaml`. If you notice a relevant
  article was missed, add the phrase that should have caught it (e.g.
  a campaigner's name, a bill's short title).
- **Paywalled titles (Times, Telegraph, FT):** these mostly don't publish
  full RSS. A free workaround is Google News' search-RSS, e.g.:
  `https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=abortion+site:thetimes.co.uk&hl=en-GB&gl=GB&ceid=GB:en`
  Add one of these per issue/title combination you care about most.

## Upgrading later (optional, not free)

Keyword matching is simple and reliable but will occasionally miss
articles that are relevant without using an obvious keyword, or flag
ones that use a keyword in an unrelated context. If that becomes a real
problem, add an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` secret (from console.anthropic.com)
and the script will automatically use Claude to classify articles more
intelligently instead of just keyword-matching — at a cost of roughly
£10–£35/month at a few hundred articles/day. This is a one-secret
change; no code editing required.

## What this does NOT cover

- **Paywalled full-text** (Times/Telegraph/FT article bodies) — only
  headlines/snippets, by design, to stay within copyright limits.
- **Social media (X, Facebook, etc.)** — this is the news half only.
  The social monitoring half needs separate setup (see the earlier
  report) because of API costs and access restrictions on those platforms.
- **Live/instant alerts** — this checks hourly, which is close to live
  but not second-by-second.
